    },
    {
      "itemIndex": 24,
      "str": "t",
      "x": 435.17,
      "y": 603.51,
      "width": 3.6,
      "height": 9.96,
      "right": 438.77,
      "visualLineId": 8,
      "inferredColumn": null
    },
    {
      "itemIndex": 25,
      "str": ". This inherently",
      "x": 438.77,
      "y": 603.51,
      "width": 65.58,
      "height": 9.96,
      "right": 504.35,
      "visualLineId": 8,
      "inferredColumn": null
    },
    {
      "itemIndex": 26,
      "str": "sequential nature precludes parallelization within training examples, which becomes critical at longer",
      "x": 108,
      "y": 592.6,
      "width": 396.17,
      "height": 9.96,
      "right": 504.17,
      "visualLineId": 9,
      "inferredColumn": null
    },
    {
      "itemIndex": 27,
      "str": "sequence lengths, as memory constraints limit batching across examples. Recent work has achieved",
      "x": 108,
      "y": 581.69,
      "width": 396,
      "height": 9.96,
      "right": 504,
      "visualLineId": 10,
      "inferredColumn": null
    },
    {
      "itemIndex": 28,
      "str": "significant improvements in computational efficiency through factorization tricks [21] and conditional",
      "x": 108,
      "y": 570.78,
      "width": 396,
      "height": 9.96,
      "right": 504,
      "visualLineId": 11,
      "inferredColumn": null
    },
    {
      "itemIndex": 29,
      "str": "computation [32], while also improving model performance in case of the latter. The fundamental",
      "x": 108,
      "y": 559.88,
      "width": 396,
      "height": 9.96,
      "right": 504,
      "visualLineId": 12,
      "inferredColumn": null
    },
    {
      "itemIndex": 30,
      "str": "constraint of sequential computation, however, remains.",
      "x": 108,
      "y": 548.97,
      "width": 222.52,
      "height": 9.96,
      "right": 330.52,
      "visualLineId": 13,
      "inferredColumn": null
    },
    {
      "itemIndex": 31,
      "str": "Attention mechanisms have become an integral part of compelling sequence modeling and transduc-",
      "x": 107.64,
      "y": 532.58,
      "width": 398.01,
      "height": 9.96,
      "right": 505.66,
      "visualLineId": 14,
      "inferredColumn": null
    },
    {
      "itemIndex": 32,
      "str": "tion models in various tasks, allowing modeling of dependencies without regard to their distance in",
      "x": 108,
      "y": 521.67,
      "width": 396,
      "height": 9.96,
      "right": 504,
      "visualLineId": 15,
      "inferredColumn": null
    },
    {
      "itemIndex": 33,
      "str": "the input or output sequences [2, 19]. In all but a few cases [27], however, such attention mechanisms",
      "x": 108,
      "y": 510.76,
      "width": 396,
      "height": 9.96,
      "right": 504,
      "visualLineId": 16,
      "inferredColumn": null
    },
    {
      "itemIndex": 34,
      "str": "are used in conjunction with a recurrent network.",
      "x": 108,
      "y": 499.85,
      "width": 195.79,
      "height": 9.96,
      "right": 303.79,
      "visualLineId": 17,
      "inferredColumn": null
    },
    {
      "itemIndex": 35,
      "str": "In this work we propose the Transformer, a model architecture eschewing recurrence and instead",
      "x": 108,
      "y": 483.46,
      "width": 396,
      "height": 9.96,
      "right": 504,
      "visualLineId": 18,
      "inferredColumn": null
    },
    {
      "itemIndex": 36,
      "str": "relying entirely on an attention mechanism to draw global dependencies between input and output.",
      "x": 108,
      "y": 472.55,
      "width": 397.74,
      "height": 9.96,
      "right": 505.74,
      "visualLineId": 19,
      "inferredColumn": null
    },
    {
      "itemIndex": 37,
      "str": "The Transformer allows for significantly more parallelization and can reach a new state of the art in",
      "x": 107.69,
      "y": 461.64,
      "width": 396.31,
      "height": 9.96,
      "right": 504,
      "visualLineId": 20,
      "inferredColumn": null
    },
    {
      "itemIndex": 38,
      "str": "translation quality after being trained for as little as twelve hours on eight P100 GPUs.",
      "x": 108,
      "y": 450.73,
      "width": 344.36,
      "height": 9.96,
      "right": 452.36,
      "visualLineId": 21,
      "inferredColumn": null
    },
    {
      "itemIndex": 39,
      "str": "",
      "x": 108,
      "y": 419.72,
      "width": 0,
      "height": 0,
      "right": 112,
      "visualLineId": null,
      "inferredColumn": null
    },
    {
      "itemIndex": 40,
      "str": "2",
      "x": 108,
      "y": 419.72,
      "width": 5.98,
      "height": 11.96,
      "right": 113.98,
      "visualLineId": 22,
      "inferredColumn": null
    },
    {
      "itemIndex": 41,
      "str": " ",
      "x": 113.98,
      "y": 419.72,
      "width": 11.96,
      "height": 0,
      "right": 125.93,
      "visualLineId": 22,
      "inferredColumn": null
    },
    {
      "itemIndex": 42,
      "str": "Background",
      "x": 125.93,
      "y": 419.72,
      "width": 62.9,
      "height": 11.96,
      "right": 188.83,
      "visualLineId": 22,
      "inferredColumn": null
    },
    {
      "itemIndex": 43,
      "str": "",
      "x": 107.69,
      "y": 395.04,
      "width": 0,
      "height": 0,
      "right": 111.69,
      "visualLineId": null,
      "inferredColumn": null
    },
    {
      "itemIndex": 44,
      "str": "The goal of reducing sequential computation also forms the foundation of the Extended Neural GPU",
      "x": 107.69,
      "y": 395.04,
      "width": 396.31,
      "height": 9.96,
      "right": 504,
      "visualLineId": 23,
      "inferredColumn": null
    },
    {
      "itemIndex": 45,
      "str": "[16], ByteNet [18] and ConvS2S [9], all of which use convolutional neural networks as basic building",
      "x": 108,
      "y": 384.13,
      "width": 396,
      "height": 9.96,
      "right": 504,
      "visualLineId": 24,
      "inferredColumn": null
    },
    {
      "itemIndex": 46,
      "str": "block, computing hidden representations in parallel for all input and output positions. In these models,",
      "x": 108,
      "y": 373.22,
      "width": 397.24,
      "height": 9.96,
      "right": 505.24,
      "visualLineId": 25,
      "inferredColumn": null
    },
    {
      "itemIndex": 47,
      "str": "the number of operations required to relate signals from two arbitrary input or output positions grows",
      "x": 108,
      "y": 362.31,
      "width": 396,
      "height": 9.96,
      "right": 504,
      "visualLineId": 26,
      "inferredColumn": null
    },
    {
      "itemIndex": 48,
      "str": "in the distance between positions, linearly for ConvS2S and logarithmically for ByteNet. This makes",
      "x": 108,
      "y": 351.4,
      "width": 396,
      "height": 9.96,
      "right": 504,
      "visualLineId": 27,
      "inferredColumn": null
    },
    {
      "itemIndex": 49,
      "str": "it more difficult to learn dependencies between distant positions [12]. In the Transformer this is",
      "x": 108,
      "y": 340.5,
      "width": 396,
      "height": 9.96,
      "right": 504,
      "visualLineId": 28,
      "inferredColumn": null
    },
    {
      "itemIndex": 50,
      "str": "reduced to a constant number of operations, albeit at the cost of reduced effective resolution due",
      "x": 108,
      "y": 329.59,
      "width": 396,
      "height": 9.96,
      "right": 504,
      "visualLineId": 29,
      "inferredColumn": null
    },
    {
      "itemIndex": 51,
      "str": "to averaging attention-weighted positions, an effect we counteract with Multi-Head Attention as",
      "x": 108,
      "y": 318.68,
      "width": 396,
      "height": 9.96,
      "right": 504,
      "visualLineId": 30,
      "inferredColumn": null
    },
    {
      "itemIndex": 52,
      "str": "described in section 3.2.",
      "x": 108,
      "y": 307.77,
      "width": 96.57,
      "height": 9.96,
      "right": 204.57,
      "visualLineId": 31,
      "inferredColumn": null
    },
    {
      "itemIndex": 53,
      "str": "Self-attention, sometimes called intra-attention is an attention mechanism relating different positions",
      "x": 108,
      "y": 291.38,
      "width": 396,
      "height": 9.96,
      "right": 504,
      "visualLineId": 32,
      "inferredColumn": null
    },
    {
      "itemIndex": 54,
      "str": "of a single sequence in order to compute a representation of the sequence. Self-attention has been",
      "x": 108,
      "y": 280.47,
      "width": 396,
      "height": 9.96,
      "right": 504,
      "visualLineId": 33,
      "inferredColumn": null
    },
    {
      "itemIndex": 55,
      "str": "used successfully in a variety of tasks including reading comprehension, abstractive summarization,",
      "x": 108,
      "y": 269.56,
      "width": 397.25,
      "height": 9.96,
      "right": 505.25,
      "visualLineId": 34,
      "inferredColumn": null
    },
    {
      "itemIndex": 56,
      "str": "textual entailment and learning task-independent sentence representations [4, 27, 28, 22].",
      "x": 108,
      "y": 258.65,
      "width": 355.12,
      "height": 9.96,
      "right": 463.12,
      "visualLineId": 35,
      "inferredColumn": null
    },
    {
      "itemIndex": 57,
      "str": "End-to-end memory networks are based on a recurrent attention mechanism instead of sequence-",
      "x": 108,
      "y": 242.26,
      "width": 397.65,
      "height": 9.96,
      "right": 505.65,
      "visualLineId": 36,
      "inferredColumn": null
    },
    {
      "itemIndex": 58,
      "str": "aligned recurrence and have been shown to perform well on simple-language question answering and",
      "x": 108,
      "y": 231.35,
      "width": 395.99,
      "height": 9.96,
      "right": 503.99,
      "visualLineId": 37,
      "inferredColumn": null
    },
    {
      "itemIndex": 59,
      "str": "language modeling tasks [34].",
      "x": 108,
      "y": 220.44,
      "width": 120.09,
      "height": 9.96,
      "right": 228.09,
      "visualLineId": 38,
      "inferredColumn": null
    },
    {
      "itemIndex": 60,
      "str": "To the best of our knowledge, however, the Transformer is the first transduction model relying",
      "x": 107.69,
      "y": 204.06,
      "width": 396.31,
      "height": 9.96,
      "right": 504,
      "visualLineId": 39,
      "inferredColumn": null
    },
    {
      "itemIndex": 61,
      "str": "entirely on self-attention to compute representations of its input and output without using sequence-",
      "x": 108,
      "y": 193.15,
      "width": 397.66,
      "height": 9.96,
      "right": 505.66,
      "visualLineId": 40,
      "inferredColumn": null
    },
    {
      "itemIndex": 62,
      "str": "aligned RNNs or convolution. In the following sections, we will describe the Transformer, motivate",
      "x": 108,
      "y": 182.24,
      "width": 396,
      "height": 9.96,
      "right": 504,
      "visualLineId": 41,
      "inferredColumn": null
    },
    {
      "itemIndex": 63,
      "str": "self-attention and discuss its advantages over models such as [17, 18] and [9].",
      "x": 108,
      "y": 171.33,
      "width": 309.35,
      "height": 9.96,
      "right": 417.35,
      "visualLineId": 42,
      "inferredColumn": null
    },
    {
